SECTION 4 — DETAILED NARRATION OF FACTS
----------------------------------------------------------------

The complainant, Ravi Kumar Sharma, states as follows:

I had entered into a business agreement with the accused Suresh
Reddy on 12/01/2026 for a joint investment in a real estate
project at Gachibowli, Hyderabad. I transferred a sum of
Rs. 12,50,000/- (Rupees Twelve Lakhs Fifty Thousand only) to
the accused's bank account (SBI A/c: XXXX7842) via RTGS on
12/01/2026 (Transaction Ref: UTIB0000X3421).

The accused promised to register the joint property in my name
within 60 days of receiving the amount.

Upon enquiry, I discovered that:
  (i)  The property shown to me does not belong to the accused.
  (ii) The bank account was opened using forged documents.
  (iii) A second person, identified as Ramu @ Ramesh, assisted
        in creating fraudulent property papers.

On 05/06/2026, when I confronted the accused at the SBI branch,
Ameerpet, the accused threatened me and refused to return the
money or execute any property documents.

I have been cheated of Rs. 12,50,000/- through criminal
conspiracy and forgery.

